# Catalogue Service
error-arepo-add-disabled = Your company has turned off adding new sources. You can still use the agents already in your library.
error-arepo-branch-invalid = That protected version name isn't valid. Use a name of up to 255 characters.
error-arepo-commit-invalid = That version marker isn't valid. It must be exactly 40 lowercase letters or numbers.
error-arepo-duplicate = ordin is already reading that source.
error-arepo-host-unsupported = ordin can only read sources from GitHub or from a site your company has approved.
error-arepo-name-invalid = That web address isn't a source ordin can read. Check it and try again.
error-arepo-remove-not-own = Only sources you added yourself can be removed or renamed.
error-arepo-signed-merges-mismatch = The signed-merge setting doesn't fit this source. Check the setting and try again.
error-cat-branch-exists = A draft with that name already exists. Choose another name.
error-cat-check-failed = A check on this item failed. Try again.
error-cat-check-unavailable = The item couldn't be added because ordin couldn't run its checks. Try again in a moment.
error-cat-fetch-failed = ordin couldn't fetch that source. Try again.
error-cat-format-changed = The item couldn't be added because the way the source is laid out has changed.
error-cat-format-unknown = ordin doesn't recognise how this source is laid out.
error-cat-lifecycle-unknown = ordin can't find that stage plan. It may have been removed.
error-cat-merge-unsigned = This change isn't signed, and the source requires signed changes.
error-cat-name-invalid = That name isn't valid. Use a short name with no special control characters.
error-cat-no-read-access = You don't have access to read that source. Sign in with an account that does.
error-cat-no-review-right = You don't have permission to review this source, so you can't open a working copy of it.
error-cat-part-unknown = ordin can't find that item. It may have been removed.
error-cat-probe-expired = That check has expired. Start it again.
error-cat-profile-key-reserved = The name "ordin" is kept for the catalogue that comes with ordin. Choose another name.
error-cat-query-invalid = Your search is too long. Shorten it to 500 characters or fewer.
error-cat-repository-limit = ordin already reads 10 sources, the most it can. Remove one of yours before you add another.
error-cat-repository-too-large = The item couldn't be added because the source is too large.
error-cat-repository-unknown = ordin can't find that source. It may have been removed.
error-cat-requirements-invalid = The requirements list needs between 1 and 50 entries, each under 2,000 characters.
error-cat-sign-in-needed = Sign in to GitHub again.
error-cat-store-failed = ordin couldn't save or read the catalogue. Try again.
error-cat-unreachable = ordin can't reach that source. Check your internet connection and try again.
error-cat-withdrawn-list-unreadable = ordin couldn't read the list of withdrawn items, so it was left unchanged.
error-life-choices-invalid = A step needs between 2 and 4 choices.
error-life-days-out-of-range = Days to answer must be left empty or be a number from 1 to 365.
error-life-place-invalid = A stage's handover place isn't valid. For Jira, use a secure address on atlassian.net of up to 2,048 characters.
error-life-role-invalid = A role must be between 1 and 200 characters.
error-life-send-back-not-earlier = A send-back must go to an earlier stage. Choose a stage that comes before this one.
error-life-send-back-rounds-out-of-range = The number of send-back rounds must be from 1 to 10.
error-life-slack-channel-invalid = A stage's Slack channel isn't valid. Check its name and try again.
error-life-stages-invalid = A plan needs between 1 and 30 stages, each with its own name of 1 to 80 characters.
error-life-stage-backward = A stage can't lead back to an earlier one. Use a send-back for that.
error-life-stage-unreachable = Every stage must be reachable from the first. Connect or remove the stage that is left out.
error-part-commit-invalid = That version marker isn't valid. It must be exactly 40 lowercase letters or numbers.
error-part-duplicate = The item couldn't be added because it is already in the catalogue.
error-part-kind-unknown = That kind of item isn't recognised. Choose one from the list.
error-part-supersedes-invalid = An item can only replace one of the same kind from the same source, and each item can be replaced only once.
error-part-version-invalid = That version number isn't valid. Use a number like 1.2.0.
error-part-withdrawal-final = A withdrawn item can't be brought back. Add it again as a new version.
error-vocab-code-invalid = That short name isn't valid. Use 1 to 64 lowercase letters, numbers or hyphens, and one that isn't already used.
error-vocab-description-too-long = That description is too long. Keep it to 1,000 characters or fewer.
error-vocab-label-invalid = That label must be between 1 and 120 characters.
error-wdl-append-only = Withdrawal records can't be changed or deleted once written.
error-wdl-reason-invalid = The reason must be between 1 and 1,000 characters.
error-wdl-replacement-incomplete = Give both the replacement name and its version, or leave both empty.
error-wdl-version-digest-mismatch = Give both the item version and its content check, or leave both empty.
